1. Refactor server.py: eliminate comments, collapse ClankServer into the HTTPServer role
    [x] 'content/backend/server.py': Strip all comments and docstrings
        - remove module docstring
        - remove _shape_kb_emission docstring
        - remove _Handler class docstring
        - remove four section-divider comment lines (# ------ GET, # ------ POST, # ------ helpers, # ------ routes)
        - remove ClankServer class docstring
        - prohibition: no '#' comments, no '""" ... """' docstrings remain
    [x] 'content/backend/server.py': ClankServer extends http.server.HTTPServer directly
        - ClankServer.__init__ accepts ingestion, kb_service, prompt_service, port, gpu_box_url; stores them; calls super().__init__(("127.0.0.1", port), _Handler)
        - ClankServer.run() calls self.serve_forever() wrapped in try/except KeyboardInterrupt, finally self.server_close()
        - ClankServer no longer creates a separate HTTPServer instance
        - ClankServer no longer bolts attributes onto a separate server object
    [x] 'content/backend/server.py': _Handler remains as the per-connection SimpleHTTPRequestHandler
        - _Handler.__init__ passes directory=str(_FRONTEND_DIR) to super
        - all route methods (do_GET, do_POST, _handle_boot, _handle_char, _forward_gpu_box) and helpers (_send_plain, _send_json) stay on _Handler
        - _Handler accesses services via self.server.<attr> (native http.server wiring, now resolves to ClankServer)
        - _shape_kb_emission stays as a module-level function
        - _FRONTEND_DIR, GPU_BOX_URL, PORT, GPU_BOX_PATHS stay as module-level constants
    [x] 'content/clank-server.py': no changes
    [x] 'content/backend/__init__.py': no changes

